[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Someone built a tool that takes any GitHub repo or a website and hands you back the prompt you would need to type to vibe code that project from scratch. It\'s called Git Reverse. It\'s open source and it\'s already garnered more than 1,000 stars on GitHub. So, the idea is basically inverting the vibe coding'

[00:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'workflow. Normally, you would write a prompt and cursor or Claude code or Codex turns it into a project, but Git Reverse goes the other direction. You paste a GitHub URL or a website URL and it gives you one short conversational'

[00:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'prompt that you can use to create that project. is pretty neat and the way it gathers context is by pulling three things: the repo\'s metadata, the root file tree at depth one, and the readme file. That\'s it. You can use it on the official Git Reverse website or you can'

[00:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'clone the repo and run it yourself. The quick reverse endpoint supports four providers: Grok, Open Router, Azure Open AI, and Google AI Studio. You just need to set the Git Reverse quick LLM key to pin one or leave it on auto and it uses'

[00:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'whichever key it finds first. And I tried running it on the Better Stack website and honestly, the results were pretty neat. It gave me a very detailed prompt and accurately identified our core product offering and the style of our brand. And not only that, but it'

[01:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'also produced a full-blown design file filled with descriptions about which colors to use and what characteristics to focus on. So, pretty cool. But, my favorite detail is the URL trick. Take any GitHub link and replace hub with reverse and it just works out of the'

[01:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'box. So, it\'s a pretty neat tool and if you need some inspiration for a starter prompt or maybe if you just want to see how your LLM describes your own project. And if you want to stay up to date with the latest open source tools and frameworks, be sure to subscribe to the'

[01:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Better Stack channel.'
